From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Astrovsky <astrouski@google.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: support MLO link STA lookup and link_id in
 mgmt_tx

In an AP MLD, management frames (such as Action frames, BSS Transition,
and TWT frames) are frequently sent to a peer station's Link MAC address
rather than its MLD MAC address.

Previously, ieee80211_mgmt_tx() only called sta_info_get_bss(sdata, mgmt->da),
which only looks up stations by MLD MAC address. When mgmt->da is a link
address, sta lookup failed (sta == NULL), causing mlo_sta to evaluate to
false.

Fix this by adding a fallback to link_sta_info_get_bss(sdata, mgmt->da)
when sta_info_get_bss() fails. Furthermore, honor params->link_id when
explicitly provided by user-space (via NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID) to select
the designated link for transmission.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Astrovsky <astrouski@google.com>
---
 net/mac80211/offchannel.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/mac80211/offchannel.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/offchannel.c
@@ -858,6 +858,11 @@ int ieee80211_mgmt_tx(struct wiphy *wiph
 
 		rcu_read_lock();
 		sta = sta_info_get_bss(sdata, mgmt->da);
+		if (!sta) {
+			struct link_sta_info *link_sta = link_sta_info_get_bss(sdata, mgmt->da);
+			if (link_sta)
+				sta = link_sta->sta;
+		}
 		mlo_sta = sta && sta->sta.mlo;
 
 		if (!ieee80211_is_action(mgmt->frame_control) ||
@@ -922,7 +927,7 @@ int ieee80211_mgmt_tx(struct wiphy *wiph
 
 		rcu_read_lock();
 
-		if (ieee80211_vif_is_mld(&sdata->vif) && mlo_sta &&
+		if (ieee80211_vif_is_mld(&sdata->vif) &&
 		    ether_addr_equal(sdata->vif.addr, mgmt->sa)) {
 			unsigned long links = sdata->vif.active_links;
 
@@ -934,7 +939,12 @@ int ieee80211_mgmt_tx(struct wiphy *wiph
 				if (!chanctx_conf)
 					continue;
 
-				if (params->chan == chanctx_conf->def.chan) {
+				if (params->link_id >= 0) {
+					if (params->link_id == link) {
+						link_id = link;
+						break;
+					}
+				} else if (params->chan == chanctx_conf->def.chan) {
 					link_id = link;
 					break;
 				}
